### 💡 Intuition & Approach
Recursively traverse a hierarchical neural network module tree to collect all registered weight and bias parameter identifiers.

### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation
```python
def autograd_l07_recursive_parameter_collection(module_hierarchy: dict) -> list:
    params = []
    def dfs(obj):
        if isinstance(obj, dict):
            if 'params' in obj and isinstance(obj['params'], list):
                params.extend(obj['params'])
            for v in obj.values(): dfs(v)
        elif isinstance(obj, list):
            for it in obj: dfs(it)
    dfs(module_hierarchy)
    return sorted(list(set(params)))
```

